From: Abdalla Ashry <abdallah.ashry@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: fix VCCIO4 supply on NanoPi R2S

The VCCIO4 domain (GMAC RGMII-M1 pins) is powered from VDD_PHY_IO,
which is fed by the 3.3 V VCC_IO rail on both the NanoPi R2S and the
R2S Plus (the optional 2.5 V LDO is not populated). The schematics
and the FriendlyElec vendor device tree agree. Declaring 1.8 V puts
the pads in 1.8 V mode on a 3.3 V rail, so point vccio4-supply at
vcc_io_33.

Signed-off-by: Abdalla Ashry <abdallah.ashry@hotmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3328-nanopi-r2s.dts
@@ -299,7 +299,7 @@
 	vccio1-supply = <&vcc_io_33>;
 	vccio2-supply = <&vcc18_emmc>;
 	vccio3-supply = <&vcc_io_sdio>;
-	vccio4-supply = <&vcc_18>;
+	vccio4-supply = <&vcc_io_33>;
 	vccio5-supply = <&vcc_io_33>;
 	vccio6-supply = <&vcc_io_33>;
 	status = "okay";
